                <pb facs="0430" n="365" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg365"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.9111/557: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Merriam</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-19T17:00:00+03:25">May 19, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 19—1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. Department’s telegram 25, May 18, 6 p.m. Saw Foreign Minister this afternoon.
                    He was hesitant about stating Iranian position in writing but agreed to consider
                    the request and to inform me of decision.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Merriam</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
